WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.799
Okay guys, this is a concept question we're being asked this time.

00:00:05.799 --> 00:00:10.759
So which of the following statements is true about the poor pressure in the following soil

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:13.880
sample during each case?

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:21.519
For case A, we can see is sand fill with saturated soil beneath the groundwater level.

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:25.760
Case B is sand fill where the soil is dry.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:33.160
And case C is where the sand fill has saturated soil and is above the groundwater level.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:37.960
And we can choose between any of these combinations that we see here.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:44.359
Now the answer to this question is A. And the reason for that is depicted here in the

00:00:44.359 --> 00:00:50.079
image, which you can see at this following link if you want more information.

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:55.739
But essentially in dry soil, the poor pressure is going to be zero, which is our case

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:02.759
B. Above the groundwater table where the soil is still saturated, the poor pressure is going

00:01:02.759 --> 00:01:10.200
to be negative, which is our case C. And below the groundwater table, poor pressure is going

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:19.359
to be positive, which is our case A. So in this case, it's correct to say that case A positive

00:01:19.359 --> 00:01:26.519
is greater than case B, zero, is greater than case C, negative.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.620
And that's it.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.079
This is just a question about poor pressure.

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:36.120
You'd have to know some geotechnical theory to get this one right.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.799
I'm not sure there's much in the manual that's going to help you, but that's just

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.480
how some concept questions go.
